' Real host-function bridge machinery -- builds fission/native_runtime/
' host_bridge.c into a real ELF64 relocatable object file (see that
' file's own header comment, and fission/amir/lower_x86_64.abas's own
' Fission_X86_64HostFunctionTable comment, for the full design). This is
' the ONE place gcc/g++ is invoked as part of THIS project's own build --
' a one-time, development-time step, exactly like compiling any other
' C++ source in this repo (ArcoFission itself, arco_runtime_core.a, ...)
' -- an end user's own ArcoBASIC program compile never shells out to it,
' only to this project's own Fusion (fission/amir/fusion_linker.abas)
' consuming the resulting `.o` via fission/amir/elf_object.abas.
'
' Deliberately NOT built through BuildTarget's own general Compile+Link/
' Archive machinery (that class always chains a Link or Archive action
' after compiling, and this needs neither -- just the raw, single `.o`
' fission/cli/compile_to_x86_64.abas reads directly at a well-known
' path) -- a single, explicit Compile action instead, the same
' RIVET.Graph.Action shape every other real Rivet target in this
' project's own build graph already uses.
'
' Reuses RIVET.Toolchain.DetectCxx()'s own real, absolute compiler
' detection (rather than a bare "gcc"/"cc" name, which the underlying
' execution mechanism cannot PATH-resolve itself) -- `host_bridge.c` is
' deliberately written in a C-compatible dialect (see that file's own
' header comment: freestanding, no C++-only features), and `-x c` forces
' real C compilation regardless of whether g++ or clang++ was actually
' detected, confirmed byte-for-byte identical to a direct `gcc` invocation
' via a real probe.
FUNCTION Fission_RivetBuildHostBridge()
    sourcePath = "fission/native_runtime/host_bridge.c"
    outputPath = ".rivet/fission-native-runtime/host_bridge.o"
    detected = RIVET.Toolchain.DetectCxx()
    IF !detected.Found THEN
        ignored = RIVET.Log.Error("no C/C++ compiler found to build fission/native_runtime/host_bridge.c (the real host-function bridge)")
    END IF
    ' -msse4.1: real floating-point support (Fission_HostFormatDouble)
    ' needs `roundsd` (SSE4.1, real hardware on every x86-64 CPU sold
    ' since ~2008) for correctly-rounded truncation/round-to-nearest-even
    ' -- there is no software fallback path, this backend's whole
    ' "no bignum/dtoa library" design depends on the real instruction.
    args = ["-x", "c", "-ffreestanding", "-fno-stack-protector", "-fno-pic", "-fno-pie", "-fno-asynchronous-unwind-tables", "-nostdlib", "-O1", "-msse4.1", "-c", sourcePath, "-o", outputPath]
    spec = { Type: "Compile", Target: "fission-native-runtime-host-bridge", DisplayName: sourcePath,
             Inputs: [sourcePath], Outputs: [outputPath],
             Tool: detected.Path, ToolVersion: "host-bridge/2/" + detected.Version,
             Arguments: args, Dependencies: [], OriginFunction: "Fission_RivetBuildHostBridge" }
    actionId = RIVET.Graph.Action(spec)
    RETURN {OutputPath: outputPath, FinalActionId: actionId}
END FUNCTION
